We build and test the application, containerize it using Docker, store the image in ECR,
deploy it on ECS using a task definition and service, expose it through an Application Load Balancer with auto-scaling enabled,
and map the domain using Route 53 for user access.


*****************************************************************
flow of tasks performed while deploying app in ECS

developer Code
   |
Build & Test (Maven / Gradle)
   |
Docker Build (app → image)
   |
Push to AWS ECR (image repository)
   |
ECS Task Definition (CPU, memory, ports, image)
   |
ECS Service (keeps containers running)
   |
Application Load Balancer
   |
Target Group (registered ECS tasks)
   |
ECS Containers running application
   |
Auto Scaling (scale up/down containers) (scale-in -> remove task from ECS cluster) (scale-out -> add new tasks to ECS cluster)
                                        (cooling period -> wait particular time before adding remove tasks from/to ECS)
   |
Route 53 → domain → ALB
   |
Users access application

